      },
      "text": "Iguazú Falls"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:9d160262ccf40bb8",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e94a996a1733ac3cde6379131caf9754422c45f0632e07fda222c4f8676166f5",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-0c9cd3aa-38d8-4e78-85c2-7fba7217988e",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Iguazú to Buenos Aires"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "dc0178094608420a1f014ff723c8292d620f1063c6c683c16b9e0979824eed25",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-0c9cd3aa-38d8-4e78-85c2-7fba7217988e",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to Puerto Iguazú Airport for your flight to Buenos Aires.\n\nOn arrival, transfer to your hotel for a two-night stay.\n\nThen take a half-day sightseeing tour of the city. The itinerary covers San Telmo, La Boca, Recoleta, Puerto Madero, Retiro, Teatro Colón, Plaza de Mayo, Avenida de Mayo and the National Congress.\n\nThe route takes you through districts that reflect different periods in the capital’s history, from the old streets of San Telmo and colourful façades of La Boca to stately Recoleta and the modern buildings of Puerto Madero. Your guide shares stories about immigrants, local legends, tango and the early 20th century, when Argentina was one of the wealthiest countries in the world.\n\nTour duration: 4 hours."
    },
